I’d like to talk about a photo I took about two months ago during a trip to Da Lat with some of my close friends.

At that time, I had been under a lot of pressure from work, so I decided to go on a short getaway to relax and recharge. We stayed in Da Lat for three days and visited several tourist attractions around the city.

The photo I’m most proud of was taken in a flower field on the outskirts of Da Lat. It was early in the morning, and two of my friends were standing among colorful flowers while the sunlight was shining gently on them. The scenery looked absolutely beautiful, so I quickly took out my phone and tried to capture the moment from a good angle.

Surprisingly, the photo turned out much better than I expected. The lighting was perfect, the colors looked vibrant, and the overall composition was really impressive. What makes me especially proud is that I didn’t use any professional camera or editing software — I simply relied on good timing and creativity.

When I showed the photo to my friends, they were really impressed and even posted it on social media right away. It received a lot of positive comments, which made me feel quite proud of my photography skills. Even now, whenever I look at that photo, it reminds me of a memorable trip and the great time I had with my friends.
